{"schema_version":2,"entity_type":"bundle","questions":[],"pools":[],"exercises":[{"client_key":"recovery_superlatives_recover","title":"Superlatives — Recupera","description":"Ricostruisci significato di gruppo, forme, spelling, articolo e irregolari.","instructions":"Prima identifica il gruppo; poi scegli la forma.","instruction_language":"it","level":"A1+","topic":"superlatives","estimated_minutes":12,"settings":{"display_mode":"one_at_a_time","feedback_timing":"question_end","show_score":false,"show_correct_answers":true,"show_explanations":true,"show_diagnostic_summary":true,"allow_retry":true},"sections":[{"client_key":"recovery_superlatives_recover_section","title":"Recupera","instructions":"Prima identifica il gruppo; poi scegli la forma.","selection_mode":"fixed","feedback_timing":"question_end","questions":[{"client_key":"recovery_superlatives_recover_teaching","type":"content_block","title":"Superlatives: scegli dentro un gruppo","prompt":"Prima di esercitarti","instructions":"Leggi le regole e osserva gli esempi.","instruction_language":"it","level":"A1+","topic":"superlatives","subtopic":"core","primary_skill":"grammar","learning_objective":"Use superlatives to identify an extreme member of a clear group with correct form, article and spelling.","difficulty":"support","content":{"educational_schema_version":1,"template_id":"educational-content-block-v1","variant":"grammar","body":"Il superlativo indica chi o che cosa occupa l'estremo dentro un gruppo. Prima controlla il significato del gruppo, poi scegli la forma.","intro":"L'errore più comune è usare una forma superlativa senza un vero gruppo oppure dimenticare the. Non basta vedere tre nomi: devi capire che stai scegliendo l'elemento con il grado massimo o minimo.","sections":[{"key":"meaning","type":"rule","title":"Serve un gruppo","body":"Usa il superlativo quando scegli o descrivi un elemento rispetto a un gruppo di almeno tre. Il gruppo può essere espresso con in/of oppure essere chiaro dal contesto.","examples":[{"text":"Of the three cafés, this one is the cheapest.","highlight":["the cheapest"]},{"text":"Leo is the tallest student in the class.","highlight":["the tallest","in the class"]}]},{"key":"short","type":"pattern","title":"Aggettivi brevi: the + -est","body":"Con molti aggettivi brevi usa the davanti alla forma in -est.","pattern":"the + short adjective-est","examples":[{"text":"small → the smallest","highlight":["the smallest"]},{"text":"fast → the fastest","highlight":["the fastest"]}]},{"key":"spelling","type":"rule","title":"Spelling","body":"Con consonante + y, y diventa i prima di -est. Con alcuni aggettivi CVC raddoppia la consonante finale.","examples":[{"text":"easy → the easiest","highlight":["the easiest"]},{"text":"happy → the happiest","highlight":["the happiest"]},{"text":"big → the biggest","highlight":["the biggest"]}]},{"key":"long","type":"rule","title":"Aggettivi più lunghi: the most","body":"Con molti aggettivi più lunghi usa the most davanti all'aggettivo senza aggiungere -est.","examples":[{"text":"comfortable → the most comfortable","highlight":["the most comfortable"]},{"text":"expensive → the most expensive","highlight":["the most expensive"]}]},{"key":"irregular","type":"comparison","title":"Good e bad","body":"Good e bad hanno forme irregolari molto frequenti.","correct":{"text":"good → the best · bad → the worst","highlight":["the best","the worst"]},"incorrect":{"text":"the goodest · the baddest","highlight":["goodest","baddest"]}},{"key":"article","type":"mistake","title":"Non perdere the","body":"Nel modello scolastico di base, il superlativo davanti a un nome usa the.","correct":{"text":"She is the youngest person on the team.","highlight":["the youngest"]},"incorrect":{"text":"She is youngest person on the team.","highlight":["youngest"]}},{"key":"two_vs_group","type":"mistake","title":"Due o più di due?","body":"Se confronti solo due elementi, normalmente serve il comparativo. Il superlativo seleziona un elemento da un gruppo di tre o più.","correct":{"text":"Of the four routes, this is the shortest.","highlight":["four","the shortest"]},"incorrect":{"text":"Of the two routes, this is the shortest.","highlight":["two","shortest"]}},{"key":"recap","type":"recap","title":"Prima di continuare","points":["Gruppo di almeno tre o riferimento collettivo chiaro.","Aggettivi brevi: the + -est.","y → iest; alcuni CVC raddoppiano.","Aggettivi lunghi: the most + adjective.","good → the best; bad → the worst.","Puoi indicare il gruppo con in/of."]}]},"grading":{"mode":"automatic","weight":0,"nearly_correct_multiplier":0.5},"feedback":{},"diagnostics":{"tested_codes":[],"fallback_error_code":null},"tags":["recovery","superlatives","recover","structured-teaching"],"foundation_links":[]},{"client_key":"recovery_sup_recover_1","type":"multiple_choice","title":"Tre percorsi","prompt":"There are three routes to school: 18, 25 and 31 minutes. The 18-minute route is ___.","instructions":"Scegli la risposta corretta.","instruction_language":"it","level":"A1+","topic":"superlatives","subtopic":"group_meaning","primary_skill":"grammar","learning_objective":"Choose a superlative from a clear group of three","difficulty":"support","content":{"options":[{"key":"a","text":"the shortest","is_correct":true},{"key":"b","text":"shorter","is_correct":false,"error_code":"SUPERLATIVE_EST"},{"key":"c","text":"the most short","is_correct":false,"error_code":"SUPERLATIVE_EST"}]},"grading":{"mode":"automatic","weight":1,"nearly_correct_multiplier":0.5},"feedback":{"explanation":"Nel gruppo di tre percorsi, uno è il più corto: the shortest."},"diagnostics":{"tested_codes":["SUPERLATIVE_EST","SUPERLATIVE_THE"],"fallback_error_code":"SUPERLATIVE_EST"},"tags":["recovery","superlatives"],"foundation_links":[]},{"client_key":"recovery_sup_recover_2","type":"select_gap","title":"Spelling nel gruppo","prompt":"Completa.","instructions":"Completa scegliendo la forma corretta.","instruction_language":"it","level":"A1+","topic":"superlatives","subtopic":"spelling","primary_skill":"grammar","learning_objective":"Apply y-to-iest and CVC doubling in superlatives","difficulty":"support","content":{"text_template":"Of these three exercises, number 2 is [[blank_1]]. Of the four boxes, the red one is [[blank_2]].","blanks":[{"key":"blank_1","accepted_answers":["the easiest"],"options":["the easiest","the easyest","the most easy"],"points":1,"feedback":{},"answer_error_mappings":[{"answer":"the easyest","error_code":"SUPERLATIVE_Y_IEST"},{"answer":"the most easy","error_code":"SUPERLATIVE_EST"}]},{"key":"blank_2","accepted_answers":["the biggest"],"options":["the biggest","the bigest","the most big"],"points":1,"feedback":{},"answer_error_mappings":[{"answer":"the bigest","error_code":"SUPERLATIVE_DOUBLE_CONSONANT"},{"answer":"the most big","error_code":"SUPERLATIVE_EST"}]}]},"grading":{"mode":"per_blank","weight":1,"nearly_correct_multiplier":0.5},"feedback":{"explanation":"Easy → the easiest; big → the biggest."},"diagnostics":{"tested_codes":["SUPERLATIVE_Y_IEST","SUPERLATIVE_DOUBLE_CONSONANT"],"fallback_error_code":"SUPERLATIVE_Y_IEST"},"tags":["recovery","superlatives"],"foundation_links":[]},{"client_key":"recovery_sup_recover_3","type":"multiple_choice","title":"Un hotel nel gruppo","prompt":"Three hotels cost €75, €95 and €160 per night. The €160 hotel is ___.","instructions":"Scegli la risposta corretta.","instruction_language":"it","level":"A1+","topic":"superlatives","subtopic":"long_adjectives","primary_skill":"grammar","learning_objective":"Use the most with a longer adjective and the article","difficulty":"support","content":{"options":[{"key":"a","text":"the most expensive","is_correct":true},{"key":"b","text":"the expensivest","is_correct":false,"error_code":"SUPERLATIVE_MOST"},{"key":"c","text":"most expensive","is_correct":false,"error_code":"SUPERLATIVE_THE"}]},"grading":{"mode":"automatic","weight":1,"nearly_correct_multiplier":0.5},"feedback":{"explanation":"Expensive usa the most."},"diagnostics":{"tested_codes":["SUPERLATIVE_MOST","SUPERLATIVE_THE"],"fallback_error_code":"SUPERLATIVE_MOST"},"tags":["recovery","superlatives"],"foundation_links":[]},{"client_key":"recovery_sup_recover_4","type":"multiple_choice","title":"Risultato irregolare","prompt":"Three students scored 54%, 79% and 92%. The 92% result is ___.","instructions":"Scegli la risposta corretta.","instruction_language":"it","level":"A1+","topic":"superlatives","subtopic":"irregular","primary_skill":"grammar","learning_objective":"Use the best as the superlative of good","difficulty":"support","content":{"options":[{"key":"a","text":"the best","is_correct":true},{"key":"b","text":"the goodest","is_correct":false,"error_code":"SUPERLATIVE_IRREGULAR"},{"key":"c","text":"the most good","is_correct":false,"error_code":"SUPERLATIVE_IRREGULAR"}]},"grading":{"mode":"automatic","weight":1,"nearly_correct_multiplier":0.5},"feedback":{"explanation":"Good → the best."},"diagnostics":{"tested_codes":["SUPERLATIVE_IRREGULAR","SUPERLATIVE_THE"],"fallback_error_code":"SUPERLATIVE_IRREGULAR"},"tags":["recovery","superlatives"],"foundation_links":[]},{"client_key":"recovery_sup_recover_5","type":"error_correction","title":"Manca una parola","prompt":"Correggi: Giulia is tallest student in our class.","instructions":"Riscrivi la frase corretta.","instruction_language":"it","level":"A1+","topic":"superlatives","subtopic":"article","primary_skill":"grammar","learning_objective":"Restore the article the in a standard superlative noun phrase","difficulty":"support","content":{"accepted_answers":["Giulia is the tallest student in our class."]},"grading":{"mode":"automatic","weight":1,"nearly_correct_multiplier":0.5},"feedback":{"explanation":"Davanti al superlativo: the tallest."},"diagnostics":{"tested_codes":["SUPERLATIVE_THE","SUPERLATIVE_EST"],"fallback_error_code":"SUPERLATIVE_THE"},"tags":["recovery","superlatives"],"foundation_links":[]},{"client_key":"recovery_sup_recover_6","type":"tr